.TH OMARCHY-DIRECTOR 1 "2026-09-19" "omarchy-director 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omarchy-director \- control an Omarchy desktop with typed natural-language plans
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omarchy-director
.RB [ --version ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B omarchy-director-ui
.RB [ --query " text " ]
.RB [ --execute ]
.br
.B omarchy-director-voice
.RI [ start | stop | toggle | cancel ]
.RB [ --preview | --yolo ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Director observes live Hyprland windows, workspaces, monitors, and installed
desktop applications. A local Jev gateway maps natural language to closed typed
choices. Deterministic Python code validates targets and executes exact Omarchy
or Hyprland operations.
.PP
Director never evaluates prompt text as shell. Plans are previewed before
execution. Reversible state is recorded under the user's XDG state directory.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the current Director-visible desktop and saved scene names as JSON.
.TP
.BI "plan --query " text
Create a bounded plan and return its token as JSON. This does not execute it.
.TP
.BI "execute --token " token
Execute a previously prepared, still-valid plan.
.TP
.B undo
Undo the most recent reversible execution once.
.TP
.BI "history [--limit " number ]
Print bounded execution history.
.TP
.B scenes list
List durable named scenes.
.TP
.BI "scenes save --name " name
Capture the current desktop as an address-free semantic scene.
.TP
.BI "scenes update --name " name
Replace an existing scene with the current desktop.
.TP
.BI "scenes apply --name " name
Restore a scene, launching identifiable missing applications when possible.
.TP
.BI "scenes delete --name " name
Delete a scene definition. The deletion can be undone from Director history.
.TP
.B doctor
Check Omarchy, Hyprland session context, and the configured Jev Unix socket.
.TP
.BI "configure --jev-socket " path
Persist an absolute Jev gateway Unix-socket path with user-only permissions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
omarchy-director plan --query 'move all terminals to workspace 3'
omarchy-director scenes save --name deep-work
omarchy-director scenes apply --name deep-work
omarchy-director configure --jev-socket /run/user/1000/jev-gateway/jev.sock
omarchy-director doctor
omarchy-director-ui --query 'activate deep-work'
.EE
.SH VOICE
Voice mode requires
.BR voxtype (1).
Preview mode transcribes and prepares the plan. YOLO requests automatic
execution, but Director still requires Enter for operations without a complete
undo boundary, including launches, screenshots, recordings, reminders, output
switching, wallpaper changes, lock, and scene application that may launch apps.
.PP
Set
.B DIRECTOR_MIC_CONTROL_BIN
to an optional executable accepting
.B start
and
.B stop
if the microphone needs an external profile or bridge controller.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JEV_SOCKET_PATH
Highest-priority Jev Unix socket. Overrides saved configuration and discovery.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration root. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
State root. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/state .
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Runtime root used for socket discovery and temporary voice transcripts.
.TP
.B OMARCHY_PATH
Omarchy installation root. When absent, launchers read the user-manager
environment and finally fall back to
.IR /usr/share/omarchy .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omarchy-director/config.json
Optional Jev socket configuration, mode 0600.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/omarchy-director/scenes.json
Durable semantic scene definitions, mode 0600.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/omarchy-director/history.json
Bounded execution and undo history, mode 0600.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/omarchy-director/
Ephemeral voice-session files.
.SH SAFETY
Omarchy plugins are unsandboxed code running as the current user. Review the
plugin before enabling it. Director does not use sudo, accept arbitrary shell,
or transmit credentials. Jev confidence is evidence, never authority.
.PP
Undo is best effort against live external state. It does not close newly
launched applications or delete screenshot, recording, or reminder artifacts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Non-zero indicates invalid arguments, unavailable
dependencies, rejected plans, stale state, or execution failure. CLI output is
JSON except for argparse help and version output.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hyprctl (1),
.BR omarchy (1),
.BR voxtype (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/ieltxu/omarchy-director/issues .
